# smpobj.msg - text for the sample scenery object (smpobj.ssl).
{100}{}{You see the village pump.}
{101}{}{An old hand pump over a stone-lined well. The handle hangs slack.}
{102}{}{An old hand pump over a stone-lined well. Water drips from the spout.}
{103}{}{An old hand pump. You know what is wrong with it: the crosshead pin has sheared.}

{110}{}{You work the handle. It swings freely and nothing comes up.}
{111}{}{You work the handle. Cold, clear water gushes from the spout.}

{120}{}{You trace the linkage. The crosshead pin has sheared, so the handle no longer lifts the rod. Now you know what to repair.}
{121}{}{The mechanism is sound. Nothing left to analyse.}

{130}{}{You check the pump for wires and springs. It is not trapped, just broken.}

{140}{}{You replace the frayed bucket rope with your own.}
{141}{}{The bucket already has a good rope.}

{150}{}{You drive out the broken pin and fit a new one. The pump works again!}
{151}{}{You fail to repair the pump.}
{152}{}{The wrench slips and you skin your knuckles on the casing.}
{153}{}{The pump is already working.}
{154}{}{*clank* *gurgle* *splash*}
